  "slug": "dark-4pcf-cb95",
  "summary": "Four preprints extend hybrid bias modelling to reconstruction, baryons and PNG bias, supporting analyses of upcoming galaxy surveys.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of simulation-informed, hybrid descriptions of tracer and gas bias in large-scale-structure analyses. A hybrid Lagrangian bias expansion is extended to post-reconstruction galaxy clustering, where a combined pre- and post-reconstruction analysis improves cosmological constraints. A hybrid effective field theory for diffuse baryons combines N-body displacements, a Lorentzian feedback suppression and linear bias. For primordial non-Gaussianity, a flexible subhalo abundance matching model fit to small-scale clustering, together with separate-universe simulations, constrains the bias parameter b_φ. CosmoMap, a conditioned 3D U-Net, differs in method, predicting hot gas temperature and electron density from dark matter fields in CAMELS IllustrisTNG. Together, these works pair simulation inputs with compact bias parameterisations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
